Indicator 1.2: Number of guidance documentation</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2018">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">Baseline: Limited capacity development activities for addressing community based waste management at district level in Turkey.</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Conducting informative stakeholder awareness raising meetings, trainings and visits.

2. Organizing the Zero Waste Management Plan workshop 

3. Providing technical support towards improvement of existing waste collection network and tools</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Increasing and disseminating the know-how of community-based action at District Level towards recycling based on the Kemer experience at the national, regional, and international scale. Project planned to prepare and distribute a booklet on Kemer Experience summarizing the data collection, analysis, strategy development and implementation towards Zero Waste based on the collaboration of citizens and municipality as well as prepare the project concept and proposals for up-scaling community based zero waste action model. 
2.Organizing a high-level panel on Local Climate Action during the Climate Council held between 21st and 25th February 2022 in Konya
3. A Study Visit to Geneva was conducted between 6th and 10th June 2022
4. In September 2022 a Best Practices Report was prepared on analysis of past and present good practices regarding river trap technologies and their applications both in Turkey and abroad by coastline municipalities in marine litter and waste management.
5. Project also prepared and delivered Zero Waste Management System Implementation Guidelines in Turkish and English, in various designs for use in schools, malls, hospitals, residential areas, airports, organized industrial zones, rural and urban areas, hotels, restaurants, cafetarias, coastlines and public institutions
6. In October 2022 an Overview Report was prepared on Increasing the Zero Waste Implementation Capacity of Districts Struggling with Fluctuating Populations based on the experience gained in Kemer District with implementation schemes to Samandag and a Guide/Booklet was prepared on community-based recycling at the District Level.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
